# M6 4a, a stage (slice 345; Codex CODEX-OPUS-345-LOWERING-TAIL-REPLY-20261110T045336Z-01 item 1): the named actual
# `p: y: 6` is a written Structure value, which the lowering does not build among the actuals of a call yet -- a limit
# of the implementation, refused where the form is recognized, not a rule of the language (the graph's executors build
# it: tests/graph/named_tail.lm2 gives 62). The next M6 item is the common constructor of a written Structure value.
Point:
    int: x 1
    int: y 2
end: Point
fn: take (Point: p; int: q 2) int
    return: p\y * 10 + q
end: take
int: code 7
if: take(p: y: 6) != 62
    code: 81
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
